From 7bda5531aaf97b9b626f9c5cd0e806f2ae5224ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:35:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 0019: put the acceleration verdict on the boot screen

Every acceleration answer this port produces landed in ioreg, in the collector's
acceleration.txt, or behind a userspace verb - a mount, a terminal or a keystroke,
and this machine has none of them inside macOS: its keyboard still does not work
after boot. N48LOG writes through IOLog, which -v prints during start(), so the
screen is the one channel left.

src/accel_boot_report.h owns whether to print (only when the fire arg was passed,
since a report on a boot that asked for nothing reads like a verdict), and the one
sentence an owner photographs, derived from the gate's verdict plus what
accelExperiment() actually returned - an errored fire says the hook was NOT
installed, a fire that never ran says so, gate 2 differs from gate 1. The block
prints after the call; navi48-report-hold=N repeats it once a second, capped at
20, and the answer publishes as Navi48,AccelReport / ,AccelReportHold.

accel_boot_report_test: 197 checks. accel_boot_report_plant.sh: 42 plants, all
caught, 0 escaped, pristine checksum unchanged.
